<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<gpx version="1.1" creator="Good Shit" xmlns="http://www.topografix.com/GPX/1/1"><trk><name>Luisenburg Felsenlabyrinth–Kösseine circuit — Luisenburg blue ascent, Kösseine and red return [planning only — not navigation-grade]</name><desc>From Luisenburg parking near Wunsiedel, climb the entrance stairs to the paid labyrinth gate and follow blue uphill through the granite maze. Continue past Kaiserfelsen and Burgstein, include the Haberstein excursion, and climb the Kösseine summit steps to Kösseinehaus. Return by red downhill and its shared lower blue section to the same gate and parking. The Burgstein platform spur is excluded. Approximate planning figures are 9.2 km, 362 m ascent/descent and three hours. Check fees, opening and weather closures; late-September 2026 cashier closing is 16:30 and the expected 18 November seasonal closure is provisional. Storms, heavy rain or snow can close the labyrinth. Stay on directed paths, do not climb off-path, leash dogs and leave strollers out of the labyrinth.

Route geometry: © OpenStreetMap contributors. OpenStreetMap walking network, Open Database License (ODbL) 1.0 — https://opendatacommons.org/licenses/odbl/1-0/; source https://www.openstreetmap.org/copyright and https://www.openstreetmap.org/api/0.6/map?bbox=11.976545,49.985687,11.999892000000001,50.015109. Changes: complete licensed source ways ordered along their literal adjacent nodes, including genuine excursions and return sections; current standard entrance footways selected; canonical display simplified using only original source vertices. No coordinate interpolation, cross-source joins or elevations. Planning only; not navigation-grade.

